In **Part 2**, we built the log ingestion pipeline (`law-sentinel-lab`, `vm-win-target`, AMA/DCR) and created our first brute-force detection rule, `Repeated Failed Windows Logons (Brute Force Signal)`, to catch repeated failed Windows sign-ins (`EventID 4625`).

In **Part 3**, we move from single-event alerts to **correlation detection**, **entity mapping**, and **SOAR automation** in Microsoft Sentinel:

1. Build a scheduled correlation rule (`4625` → `4624`) that detects multiple failed logons followed by a successful logon (`LogonType` `10` or `3`) from the same source IP against `vm-win-target`.
2. Map query output fields to Sentinel entities (`IP`, `Account`, `Host`) so analysts get clear context and attack graphs.
3. Create a Logic App playbook (`pb-incident-notify`), grant Sentinel permission to run it, attach it with an automation rule, and verify end-to-end alert delivery on **Incident ID 25**.

